module

public import
  StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FormalGeometry.Completion.AdicQuotientCompletionDerivedLimit
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FormalGeometry.DerivedCompletionRinged.GlobalSectionsCompletionGenerated
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FormalGeometry.DerivedCompletionRinged.GlobalSectionsCompletionKoszulIdentity
public import
  StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FormalGeometry.DerivedCompletionRinged.RingedSpaceDerivedSections

/-!
# `RΓ(Y, ℱ)^∧` is the derived sections of a derived limit of the adic quotients

Let `Y` be a quasi-compact locally Noetherian scheme, let `A` be a commutative ring with a ring
map `ρ : A ⟶ Γ(Y, 𝒪_Y)`, let `a_1, …, a_r ∈ A` and let `ℐ ⊂ 𝒪_Y` be the quasi-coherent sheaf of
ideals generated by their images. For a coherent `𝒪_Y`-module `ℱ` this file produces **one object
`ℒ` of `D(𝒪_Y)`** which is at the same time

* a derived limit of the tower `n ↦ ℱ/ℐⁿℱ` placed in degree zero, and
* such that `RΓ(Y, ℒ)` is the derived `(a_1, …, a_r)`-adic completion of `RΓ(Y, ℱ)` in `D(A)`.

That is the conjunction the left-hand side of [Stacks, Tag 0DXI] needs: it lets a statement about
`Hⁱ(RΓ(Y, ℒ))` for a derived limit `ℒ` of the adic quotients be read as a statement about
`Hⁱ(RΓ(Y, ℱ)^∧)`, with no derived-limit structure assumed.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Algebraization.koszulGlobalGenerator_structureGenerators` — the `i`-th chosen global
  section of `𝒪_Y` has value `ρ a_i` over the whole of `Y`.
* `Stacks.Algebraization.koszulIdealSheafData_structureGenerators_congr` — the ideal sheaf
  `(ρ a_1, …, ρ a_r)𝒪_Y` depends only on the ideal `(a_1, …, a_r)` of `A`, so it is `I𝒪_Y` and not
  an artefact of the chosen presentation of `I`.
* `Stacks.Algebraization.exists_isDerivedLimit_and_iso_derivedCompletion_derivedSections` — **the
  displayed statement.**

## The two inputs

*The derived limit* is `Stacks.Algebraization.isDerivedLimit_adicQuotientSystem_completion`, the
two halves of [Stacks, Tag 0A0K] at the Čech completion `ℱ^∧` of [Stacks, Tag 099B].

*The identity `RΓ(Y, ℱ)^∧ = RΓ(Y, ℱ^∧)`* is [Stacks, Tag 0BLX],
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.nonempty_iso_derivedCompletion_derivedGlobalSections`, at the
reflector of [Stacks, Tag 099F]; the Čech completion is identified with that reflector by
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.exists_iso_derivedCompletion_completionFunctor_obj`, so the one
object `ℒ` serves both. Both derived global-sections functors of the identity are then replaced by
the derived sections of the ringed space underlying `Y`, using
`Stacks.Cohomology.RingedSpaceSections.derivedSectionsOverIsoDerivedGlobalSectionsOverUnbounded`.

## Implementation notes

*Why the statement names `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.completionFunctor` nowhere.* Both the
reflector `(-)^∧` of [Stacks, Tag 099F] and the Čech model of [Stacks, Tag 099B] appear in the
proof, and the reflector cannot even be written down without the `IsRightAdjoint` instance, which
instance search does not find at the ringed site of opens of a concrete scheme: unifying
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.opensRingedSite ?Rc` with the site of a given scheme asks it to recover a
structure from a projection. Both are therefore existentially quantified away, and the object the
statement produces is named only by the two properties it has.

*The scalars.* The ring map is given on the ringed space, as `A ⟶ 𝒪_Y(⊤)`; the ringed-site
presentation `Γ(𝒞, 𝒪_Y)` it induces is `Stacks.Cohomology.RingedSpaceSections.siteScalars`, and
the generators of the ideal sheaf are the images of `a_1, …, a_r` under it.

*The completeness instances.* The coproduct of the Koszul system and the products of the Hom
tower, which make the derived colimit and the derived limits of [Stacks, Tag 0A0E] exist, are
produced at the scheme's own spelling of the category of modules and transported by
`inferInstanceAs`; they are not hypotheses.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 099B](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/099B)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 099F](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/099F)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0A0E](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0A0E)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0A0K](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0A0K)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BLX](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BLX)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0DXI](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0DXI)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits CategoryTheory.Pretriangulated
open Opposite TopologicalSpace
open AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite

universe u

attribute [local instance] AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.submoduleCompleteLattice

namespace Stacks.Algebraization

attribute [local instance] modulesEnoughInjectives

-- `HasDerivedCategory.standard` at a raised priority. The library also carries the global
-- instance `StacksDraft.DerivedCategory.LocallySmall.hasDerivedCategory`, which names the
-- derived category of sheaves of modules at the hom universe `u` rather than `u + 1`; the
-- statements this file consumes and produces are all at `u + 1`, so the standard instance has
-- to win, and it has to be *that* instance and not a local alias of it, so that the derived
-- categories of this file and of its consumers are the same term and not merely the same type.
attribute [local instance 100000] HasDerivedCategory.standard

section Main

variable (Y : Scheme.{u}) [IsLocallyNoetherian Y] [CompactSpace Y] (A : Type u) [CommRing A]
  (ρ : A →+* (structureSheafRing Y.toRingedSpace).obj.obj
    (op (⊤ : Opens Y.toRingedSpace.carrier)))
  {r : ℕ} (a : Fin r → A) (ℱ : Y.Modules) [ℱ.IsCoherent]

/-- The images in `Γ(𝒞, 𝒪_Y)` of the chosen elements of `A`, as the global sections generating
the ideal sheaf `(a_1, …, a_r)𝒪_Y`. -/
abbrev structureGenerators :
    Fin r → Presheaf.globalSections
      ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.opensRingedSite Y.sheaf).O.obj ⋙ forget CommRingCat.{u}) :=
  fun i ↦ globalSectionOfSections
    (Stacks.Cohomology.RingedSpaceSections.siteScalars Y.toRingedSpace A ρ (a i))

omit [IsLocallyNoetherian Y] [CompactSpace Y] in
/-- **The `i`-th chosen global section has value `ρ a_i` over the whole of `Y`.** The compatible
family `Stacks.Cohomology.RingedSpaceSections.siteScalars` builds from `ρ a_i` is the one whose
value over the terminal open is `ρ a_i`, which is
`Stacks.Cohomology.RingedSpaceSections.sectionsEval_comp_siteScalars`. -/
theorem koszulGlobalGenerator_structureGenerators (i : Fin r) :
    koszulGlobalGenerator Y (structureGenerators Y A ρ a) i = ρ (a i) :=
  (RingedSite.globalSectionVal_globalSectionOfSections
      (Stacks.Cohomology.RingedSpaceSections.siteScalars Y.toRingedSpace A ρ (a i)) (op ⊤)).trans
    (RingHom.congr_fun
      (Stacks.Cohomology.RingedSpaceSections.sectionsEval_comp_siteScalars
        Y.toRingedSpace A ρ) (a i))

omit [IsLocallyNoetherian Y] [CompactSpace Y] in
/-- **The ideal sheaf `(ρ a_1, …, ρ a_r)𝒪_Y` depends only on the ideal `(a_1, …, a_r)` of `A`.**
Two finite families of `A` spanning the same ideal generate the same quasi-coherent sheaf of
ideals, so the adic quotient tower the statements below are about is the tower of quotients by
the powers of `I𝒪_Y` and not an artefact of the chosen presentation of `I`. -/
theorem koszulIdealSheafData_structureGenerators_congr {s : ℕ} (b : Fin s → A)
    (hab : Ideal.span (Set.range a) = Ideal.span (Set.range b)) :
    koszulIdealSheafData Y (structureGenerators Y A ρ a) =
      koszulIdealSheafData Y (structureGenerators Y A ρ b) := by
  have key : ∀ {t : ℕ} (c : Fin t → A),
      Ideal.span (Set.range (koszulGlobalGenerator Y (structureGenerators Y A ρ c))) =
        Ideal.map (show A →+* Γ(Y, ⊤) from ρ) (Ideal.span (Set.range c)) := by
    intro t c
    rw [Ideal.map_span, ← Set.range_comp]
    exact congrArg (Ideal.span ∘ Set.range)
      (funext fun i ↦ koszulGlobalGenerator_structureGenerators Y A ρ c i)
  unfold koszulIdealSheafData
  rw [key a, key b, hab]

/-- **One object is both a derived limit of the adic quotients and a derived completion of the
global sections.** Let `Y` be a quasi-compact locally Noetherian scheme, `A` a commutative ring
with `ρ : A ⟶ Γ(Y, 𝒪_Y)`, `a_1, …, a_r ∈ A`, `ℐ = (ρ a_1, …, ρ a_r)𝒪_Y` and `ℱ` a coherent
`𝒪_Y`-module. Then there is an `ℒ` in `D(𝒪_Y)` such that

1. `ℒ` is a derived limit of the tower `n ↦ ℱ/ℐⁿℱ` placed in degree zero, and
2. `RΓ(Y, ℒ)` is isomorphic to the derived `(a_1, …, a_r)`-adic completion of `RΓ(Y, ℱ)`.

Part (1) is the two halves of [Stacks, Tag 0A0K] —
`Stacks.Algebraization.isDerivedLimit_adicQuotientSystem_completion` — and part (2) is
[Stacks, Tag 0BLX] at the same object. `RΓ(Y, -)` is the derived sections of the ringed space
underlying `Y` and the completion on `D(A)` is
`DerivedCompletion.derivedCompletionFunctor A a`, the derived completion along
`Ideal.span {a_1, …, a_r}`.

The ideal sheaf is `Stacks.Algebraization.koszulIdealSheafData` at those global sections, the
extension to `Y` of the ideal they span; by `Stacks.Algebraization.eq_koszulIdealSheafData` every
quasi-coherent sheaf of ideals generated by them on each affine open equals it, so fixing it is
not a hypothesis on the data. No tag attribute is attached: the statement is an assembly of two
tags, each registered where it is proved. -/
theorem exists_isDerivedLimit_and_iso_derivedCompletion_derivedSections :
    ∃ L : DerivedCategory Y.Modules,
      (∃ h : HasProduct (fun n : ℕ =>
          (adicQuotientSystem (koszulIdealSheafData Y (structureGenerators Y A ρ a)) ℱ ⋙
            DerivedCategory.singleFunctor Y.Modules 0).obj ⟨n⟩),
        @IsDerivedLimit (DerivedCategory Y.Modules) _ _ _ _ _ _
          (adicQuotientSystem (koszulIdealSheafData Y (structureGenerators Y A ρ a)) ℱ ⋙
            DerivedCategory.singleFunctor Y.Modules 0) h L) ∧
      Nonempty ((Stacks.Cohomology.DerivedSectionsOverBase.derivedSectionsOver
            Y.toRingedSpace ρ).obj L ≅
        (DerivedCompletion.derivedCompletionFunctor A a).obj
          ((Stacks.Cohomology.DerivedSectionsOverBase.derivedSectionsOver
            Y.toRingedSpace ρ).obj
              ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor Y.Modules 0).obj ℱ))) := by
  refine ⟨(RingedSite.completionFunctor (Stacks.SheafOfModules.opensRingedSite Y.sheaf)
      (structureGenerators Y A ρ a)).obj
      (DerivedCategory.Q.obj (RingedSite.singleSheafComplex
        (Stacks.SheafOfModules.opensRingedSite Y.sheaf) ℱ)),
    isDerivedLimit_adicQuotientSystem_completion Y (structureGenerators Y A ρ a) ℱ, ?_⟩
  -- the reflector of [Stacks, Tag 099F] exists at this globally generated ideal sheaf
  have hra : (ObjectProperty.ι (RingedSite.IsDerivedComplete.{u, u, u, u}
      (Stacks.SheafOfModules.opensRingedSite Y.sheaf)
      (generatedIdealSheaf (structureGenerators Y A ρ a)))).IsRightAdjoint :=
    isRightAdjoint_ι_isDerivedComplete_generatedIdealSheaf
      (Stacks.SheafOfModules.opensRingedSite Y.sheaf) (structureGenerators Y A ρ a)
  have hco : HasCoproduct ((RingedSite.koszulPowerSystem
      (Stacks.SheafOfModules.opensRingedSite Y.sheaf) (structureGenerators Y A ρ a) ⋙
        DerivedCategory.Q).obj) :=
    inferInstanceAs (HasCoproduct (show ℕ → DerivedCategory Y.Modules from
      (RingedSite.koszulPowerSystem (Stacks.SheafOfModules.opensRingedSite Y.sheaf)
        (structureGenerators Y A ρ a) ⋙ DerivedCategory.Q).obj))
  -- Tag 0BLX at the reflector, and the reflector identified with the Čech completion
  obtain ⟨e⟩ := nonempty_iso_derivedCompletion_derivedGlobalSections
    (Stacks.SheafOfModules.opensRingedSite Y.sheaf) A
    (Stacks.Cohomology.RingedSpaceSections.siteScalars Y.toRingedSpace A ρ) a
    (DerivedCategory.Q.obj (RingedSite.singleSheafComplex
      (Stacks.SheafOfModules.opensRingedSite Y.sheaf) ℱ))
  obtain ⟨eC, -⟩ := exists_iso_derivedCompletion_completionFunctor_obj
    (Stacks.SheafOfModules.opensRingedSite Y.sheaf) (structureGenerators Y A ρ a)
    (DerivedCategory.Q.obj (RingedSite.singleSheafComplex
      (Stacks.SheafOfModules.opensRingedSite Y.sheaf) ℱ))
  -- the two derived global-sections functors
  have eΓ :=
    Stacks.Cohomology.RingedSpaceSections.derivedSectionsOverIsoDerivedGlobalSectionsOverUnbounded
      Y.toRingedSpace A ρ
  -- `ℱ` in degree zero, as a complex and as an object of the derived category
  have eS := ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctorIsoCompQ Y.Modules 0).app ℱ).symm
  -- the derived global sections over `A`, applied to the comparison isomorphisms
  let F := derivedGlobalSectionsOverUnbounded (Stacks.SheafOfModules.opensRingedSite Y.sheaf) A
    (Stacks.Cohomology.RingedSpaceSections.siteScalars Y.toRingedSpace A ρ)
  exact ⟨eΓ.app _ ≪≫ F.mapIso eC.symm ≪≫ e ≪≫
    (DerivedCompletion.derivedCompletionFunctor A a).mapIso (F.mapIso eS ≪≫ (eΓ.app _).symm)⟩

end Main

end Stacks.Algebraization

end
